    "dose": "Surgical prophylaxis. Deep IM or IV: Infant over 1 month 25 mg/kg (maximum 1 g dose) as a single dose at induction of anaesthesia, repeated if necessary if surgery lasts over 3 hours. Further doses may be given every 6–8 hours postoperatively for 24 hours if necessary, or for up to 5 days in continued risk of infection. Intramuscular administration may be painful and should be avoided where possible. If IM injection is required/necessary cefazolin can be reconstituted with lidocaine 0.5%.",
