    "precautions": "Pancreatitis (see below); renal impairment; chronic hepatitis B or C; hepatic disease (see below). Pancreatitis If no suitable alternative exists, use with extreme caution in children with advanced HIV infection, previous history of pancreatitis or risk factors for pancreatitis. Hepatic disease Potentially life-threatening lactic acidosis and severe hepatomegaly with steatosis reported; caution in children with hepatomegaly, hepatitis (especially hepatitis C treated with interferon alfa and ribavirin), liver enzyme abnormalities, or risk factors for liver disease and hepatic steatosis; discontinue if rapid deterioration in liver function tests, symptomatic hyperlactataemia, progressive hepatomegaly or lactic acidosis. Exacerbation of hepatitis in patients with chronic hepatitis B may occur on discontinuation of lamivudine.",
